-- title:
--   Diamond automorphism restricted to the pole chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero natural number $M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a unit $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$. The hypothesis `hj` asserts that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNum` with coefficients pushed into $\mathbb{Q}$, lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios `intFormRatiosC ℚ ⊤` at full level; this provides the element `jAt (ΓM M H) hj` of the $q$-expansion function field $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` of the congruence subgroup `ΓM M H` attached to $M$ and $H$. Let $O =$ `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj` be the pole chart algebra of the two-chart integral model: the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over the `R p`-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $($`jAt`$)^{-1}$. The assertion is that there exists an `R p`-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $O$ such that for every $b \in O$ the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` of the Laurent series underlying $\sigma b$ equals the value at the corresponding element of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` $=$ `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (xHFunctionField M H)` of the inverse of `diamondAutHBar M H d`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` chosen to satisfy `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d` when such an automorphism exists and taken to be the identity otherwise. No divisibility relation between $p$ and $M$ is assumed.
--
--   This records that the diamond operator $\langle d\rangle$ on $X_H(M)$, read on $q$-expansions after base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, preserves the integral pole chart of the two-chart model over `R p`, so that it is induced by an automorphism of that chart algebra. It is used in the comparison of $\langle d\rangle$ with the chart immersions of the Deligne–Rapoport model (`iotaFin_comp_dia0_hom_eq_spec_map_comp_iotaFin` and `iotaInf_comp_dia0_hom_eq_spec_map_comp_iotaInf`) and in the $q$-expansion statement `exists_mul_ofPowerSeries_eq_of_diamondAutHBar_apply_eq_coeffEmb_of_level_mul`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algEquiv_chartAlgInf_forall_coeffEmb_eq_diamondAutHBar_symm.lean

